{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Gerrit change 3467 patch set 1: Verified +1, LLM-Review -1 (2 blocking). Patch set 2 addresses both: (1) new test test_unreadable_list_fails_closed_through_verification proves an unreadable list (empty or malformed REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS) yields untrusted through verify_signature; flipping the except branch to 'no list' makes both cases fail (checked). (2) secret-detection: reproduced locally with gitleaks; generic-api-key matched the env-id UUID after the identifiers REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS / trusted_keys (4 sites). These are environment ids and OpenSSH public keys, not secrets. Added a .gitleaks.toml allowlist scoped to exactly a UUID right after those two identifiers; a negative control shows a GitHub PAT and a random token under trusted_keys are still caught. Advisories: added a validate test for the untrusted MINOR finding; a keyless envelope in list mode now reads mismatch with an accurate reason; docs/manifest-signing.md is rewritten in waterish-aquamarine-bug; a config read failure failing closed is intended (ADR 0125: a malformed list fails closed), and keeping the list out of the repository rebar.toml is the ADR's stated convention."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795130125106586001,"uuid":"92f3ad21-5de7-4e02-a334-558b48ed8065"}